# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git normalizes text to LF in the object store, but `core.autocrlf=true` — the
# Windows default — rewrites it to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for source
# files and fatal for shell scripts: bash reads `set -euo pipefail\r` as an
# option named `pipefail\r` and aborts, with the stray CR scrambling the error
# message on the way out.
#
# Anything executed by an interpreter that reads the shebang, or by a Linux
# container, is therefore pinned to LF regardless of platform.
#
# Since 2026-10-10 that is every text file rather than a list of extensions.
# The list missed `.mjs`, `.sh.hbs`, `Dockerfile.hbs` and every YAML file,
# and the misses were not harmless: Vite's SSR transform looks for a hashbang
# line ending in LF only, so a CRLF one is not found, its hoisted imports land
# above it, and vitest fails to load `stack.mjs` with "SyntaxError: Invalid or
# unexpected token" while plain `node` accepts the same file.
# A list is a guess about which tool cares; LF everywhere is not. The object
# store was already LF throughout, so this changed no content -- only what a
# Windows checkout writes. The explicit rules below stay, as documentation and
# because the CRLF ones must override this line.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
*.mk        text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF — cmd.exe requires it.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Binary, never converted.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary

# The scanner service's files run inside a Linux container. A CRLF in the
# entrypoint is "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter", and in clamd.conf an unknown
# option, and either one fails after the image is built rather than before.
profiles/product/template/services/clamd/*.conf text eol=lf
profiles/product/template/services/clamd/*.yaml text eol=lf
profiles/product/template/services/clamd/fly.toml.hbs text eol=lf
